# Pinned commit SHAs for the chatbot's RAG corpus (internal/docindex/docs/),
# for git-lrc, git-lrc's wiki, LiveReview's wiki, and the public docs site
# (hexmoshomepage's pages/livereview/docs/ - what's published at
# hexmos.com/livereview/docs). LiveReview's own top-level docs/ (internal
# engineering plans, release notes, etc.) is deliberately NOT part of this
# corpus at all - see scripts/docindex/sync_docs_sources.sh.
#
# GitHub/GitLab, not any developer's machine, is the source of truth: these
# SHAs are what actually gets embedded into the binary (dev builds,
# `make build`, and Docker images alike - see
# scripts/docindex/sync_docs_sources.sh). This is normally kept current
# automatically (see check_docs_sources.py --auto, wired into every sync);
# a value here changing by hand is possible but not required.
#
# HEXMOSHOMEPAGE_DOCS_COMMIT points at a PRIVATE repo
# (git@git.apps.hexmos.com:hexmos/frontend/hexmoshomepage.git), unlike the
# 3 public GitHub sources below - any machine that builds LiveReview
# (including CI/Docker build hosts) needs SSH access to git.apps.hexmos.com
# configured for this source to sync; a missing/failing SSH key just means
# that one source is skipped (see sync_docs_sources.sh), not a build
# failure, but the content will then be stale/missing there.
#
# Checking for drift / bumping: see docs/docs-sources-pinning-plan.md, or
# run `make check-docs-sources` / `make update-docs-sources` /
# `make update-docs-sources-yes`.
GIT_LRC_COMMIT=14584106823b1597e2097fca9ff42d2d18de5417
GIT_LRC_WIKI_COMMIT=a1bb17c392a46c1f3bf6cfad6396813ccf80a1a9
LIVEREVIEW_WIKI_COMMIT=b212da48de8ecacb167f562682d2a6491a1e327f
HEXMOSHOMEPAGE_DOCS_COMMIT=4192cce20f254bdcad6146ba7a6ce98db4f8db2b
